Spec: Local Linux server identity request

Purpose:
  Provision one local P-256 server key and export only its standard proof-of-possession CSR for owner signing.

Owns:
  ./request.go
  ./request_test.go

Must:
  Require an existing protected identity directory and create private key/request files exclusively with private permissions.
  Keep the private key on its host; return only fixed completion and leave the public CSR available as a separate file.
  Preserve existing or partial identity state instead of rotating or overwriting it on repeated commands.
  Use standard P-256 PKCS8 and PKCS10 with the LinkGate device name and fsync new files and their directory.
